The program supports command line options for `--help`, `-v` (verbose mode), and `-o` (output file) to specify the output file path. If no input file is specified, the program prints usage information and exits gracefully. If an input file is provided, the program reads it line by line and processes each line to allocate memory for and initialize the arrays. The program also handles potential I/O errors and ensures efficient memory usage and minimizes potential fragmentation issues.

