Performance considerations include minimizing memory overhead and ensuring low-latency access under heavy load. Developers must carefully balance efficiency, usability, maintainability, and scalability, making informed trade-offs as necessary. Additionally, managing network latency, handling intermittent connectivity, and ensuring data consistency across nodes in a distributed environment are important engineering challenges that developers must consider when implementing this system.']

