This code block implements a record manager function that dynamically manages an in-memory data structure for storing and retrieving records. It includes functions for inserting, updating, and deleting records, as well as functions for checking the uniqueness of keys and printing all records in the linked list. The function ensures that keys remain unique and weights are non-negative, and it handles memory allocation failures gracefully using appropriate error handling mechanisms. The record structure includes an integer key, a long offset, and a double weight. The function is designed to optimize for memory usage and efficient data access patterns, taking into account the possibility of scaling with increasing data volumes. It also includes a robust concurrency model to manage simultaneous updates to the records, addressing potential race conditions and ensuring data consistency.']

