To ensure robustness and stability, the function includes checks for out-of-bounds access, memory allocation failures, and edge cases such as zero-sized arrays or very large string lengths. The function uses the third-party library `my_custom_library.h` for floating-point arithmetic, which has been observed to exhibit occasional instability in edge cases. To address this issue, the function includes alternative libraries or algorithms that can provide better reliability and accuracy.

