The `compress_image()` and `decompress_image()` functions compress and decompress an image using the specified compression algorithm, respectively. The `resize_image()` function resizes an image using nearest neighbor interpolation.

The `render_image()` function renders a still image using progressive rendering technique by updating the frame buffer with current image data and rendering the updated frame buffer to the screen. The `animate_image()` function animates an image using progressive rendering technique and a specified animation duration by updating the frame buffer with current image data, rendering the updated frame buffer to the screen at a specified animation duration, and repeating this process for all frames of the animation.

This library allows users to specify custom image and compression settings through a configuration file, which can be used to optimize the performance of the library for specific hardware capabilities and operating systems. The library also incorporates robust error handling and logging mechanisms to aid in debugging and monitoring.']

