The code also includes a mechanism to periodically monitor memory usage and trigger garbage collection if the allocated memory exceeds a specified threshold. This is done using the `garbage_collection` function, which calculates the current memory usage of the record array and compares it to the threshold. If the memory usage exceeds the threshold, the function triggers garbage collection by freeing the memory used by the record array and setting it to NULL.

