To optimize performance, this implementation considers factors such as limited memory footprint and CPU resources during memory allocation and data structure manipulation. It also includes a mechanism for garbage collection to handle memory management of `Item` structures. The trade-off between memory usage and frequent garbage collection operations is carefully balanced to ensure responsiveness during peak times while minimizing CPU usage.

