To handle potential race conditions if the function is called concurrently from multiple threads, it uses a mutex lock to ensure mutual exclusion of the critical section that modifies the record array. It also defines a compare function for the qsort function to sort the `record` array based on their offsets.

The function returns an informative error message if any memory allocation fails, and a return code indicating failure."]

