The code also includes functions for reading and writing data records to the storage system, as well as a function to traverse directories and list files and their paths up to a specified depth. Error handling is implemented to prevent out-of-bounds access and handle memory allocation failures gracefully. The system is designed to be flexible enough to accommodate diverse file system configurations and handle unexpected errors or incomplete data gracefully.

