The system's performance is optimized by minimizing memory fragmentation and ensuring efficient data retrieval, especially when dealing with large datasets. Memory usage is evaluated and strategies are explored for managing memory efficiently, possibly leveraging memory pools or custom allocators. The code is designed to be robust and flexible enough to handle file system inconsistencies and unexpected errors gracefully, while also providing a balance between efficiency and usability.']

