The function checks for memory usage and fragmentation after every 10 MB of memory has been allocated, and defragments the memory by releasing unused chunks and updating the offset array. It also prints a message to the console if the memory limit is exceeded or if the memory is nearing full.

At the end of processing, the function computes and prints the average value of all valid data points, and frees up any remaining memory using `free`. The code also includes error handling for network socket errors and uses a robust logging mechanism to track data points processed and errors encountered.

The function is designed to be modularized, supporting flexible configurations for different data types and processing priorities, allowing for future extensibility. It analyzes and reports detailed metrics on memory usage, fragmentation, and processing time to inform optimization strategies.']

